SUMMARY:Through the Adivasi Gaze
DESCRIPTION: Aabua Paika Kabu Bageya: We Won’t Let Go of Our Paika! | 26 mins |  Mundari | 2017 | India \nThis film screening and panel discussion explores the critical role of self-representation in reclaiming cultural identity. What changes when Adivasi culture is conveyed by Adivasis themselves\, rather than through an outside lens? \nThe program opens with a screening of the documentary Aabua Paika Kabu Bageya: We Won’t Let Go of Our Paika!\, centring on Paika\, a traditional Munda martial art dance form that serves as a living archive of historical struggle\, triumph\, and resilience. A panel discussion follows\, marking a fundamental shift in perspective: moving away from the historic\, colonial lens to honour the Adivasi gaze. Tribal culture\, the panel argues\, is not a static object to be documented by outsiders or kept in museums\, but a dynamic\, living identity best understood through narratives produced directly by members of the community themselves. The event concludes with an audience Q&A. \nIn collaboration with: \n \nVenue: Seminar Hall\n\n\nShifting From External Archives to Adivasi-Led Storytelling\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeE7Y1eH_Hgom8_0M8Qk_sbQsQxbmRKnKZA_jFuS6EDRwzdhA/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Sneha Mundari\, Nandini Tank\n*Event Categories*: Film
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/through-the-adivasi-gaze/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Thumbnail_TTAG.jpg
